Undo the steps from last to first:

- $2 \times 10 = 20$ (undo “divide by $10$”);
- $20 - 8 = 12$ (undo “add $8$”);
- $12^2 = 144$ (undo “square root”);
- $144 + 52 = 196$ (undo “subtract $52$”);
- $\sqrt{196} = 14$ (undo “multiply by itself”);
- $14 \times \tfrac{3}{2} = 21$ (undo “subtract a third”, which multiplied by $\tfrac{2}{3}$);
- $21 \times 7 = 147$ (undo “divide by $7$”);
- $147 \times \tfrac{4}{7} = 84$ (undo “add three quarters”, which multiplied by $\tfrac{7}{4}$);
- $84 \div 3 = 28$ (undo “multiply by $3$”).

Check forwards: $28 \to 84 \to 147 \to 21 \to 14 \to 196 \to 144 \to 12 \to 20 \to 2$.

